# TOS / Privacy acknowledgement checkboxes (ALGR)

**Source:** Linear [CURSOR-759](https://linear.app/marley/issue/CURSOR-759/new-user-tosprivacy-acknowledgement) (formerly CAL-759). Applies to **all Labs account products**.

New users must not get stuck on accept-terms because acknowledgement is only implied by clicking bolded Terms/Privacy names.

## Required UX (all sites with accounts)

On accept-terms / first-login legal gate:

1. Show **two visible checkboxes** (or equivalent explicit controls), one for **Terms of Service** and one for **Privacy Policy**.
2. **Continue** (or equivalent) stays **disabled** until **both** are checked/acknowledged.
3. Terms checkbox opens `TermsConsentPopover` (or product equivalent); agreeing in the dialog checks the Terms box. Do not treat a bare external link click as acceptance.
4. Privacy checkbox is checked after the user opens/reads Privacy (link may open `/privacy`; checking the box is the acknowledgement signal).
5. Persist Terms acceptance on the **server** (`termsAcceptedAt` + `termsVersion`) — never client-only.

## Anti-patterns

| Avoid | Why |
|-------|-----|
| Bold link text only, no checkbox | Users do not realize they must “acknowledge” |
| Single combined “I agree to Terms and Privacy” without separate controls | Ambiguous which document was reviewed |
| Continue enabled before both acknowledgements | Locks / confusion; fails CURSOR-759 |
| Checkbox that only navigates away and never records state | No durable acknowledgement |

